doc:sch-1-sec-3-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "3(2) Effect on TCF contract outworker’s entitlements" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) To avoid doubt, if: (a) a term of a modern award requires the principal of a TCF contract outworker to apply the National Employment Standards to the outworker as if the outworker were an employee; and (b) because of Division 2 of Part 6-4A of the amended Act, the outworker is taken to be an employee (being a national system employee) of the principal for the purposes of" ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 Fair work instruments etc. made before commencement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-4 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause applies in relation to:  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Amendments made by the Fair Work Amendment (Textile, Clothing and Footwear Industry) Act 2012  Part 1  Clause 5 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) a fair work instrument made before commencement; or (b) a transitional instrument as continued in existence by Schedule 3 to the Transitional Act. (2) A reference in the instrument to an employee or an employer does not include a deemed employee or a deemed employer, unless the instrument is, after commencement, varied to make it clear that the reference is intended to include a deemed employee or deemed employer. (3) This clause is not to be taken to confer a power to vary the instrument." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This clause applies in relation to:  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Amendments made by the Fair Work Amendment (Textile, Clothing and Footwear Industry) Act 2012  Part 1  Clause 5 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) a fair work instrument made before commencement; or (b) a transitional instrument as continued in existence by Schedule 3 to the Transitional Act. (2) A reference in the instrument to an employee or an employer does not include a deemed employee or a deemed employer, unless the instrument is, after commencement, varied to make it clear that the reference is intended to include a deemed employee or deemed employer. (3) This clause is not to be taken to confer a power to vary the instrument."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f793a4c7eec00a62dd516ca070eb4bcec7fb7ceb16f1da754bafbb1079a4ffdd" ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer ;
