doc:sch-1-sec-92 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "92 Application—section 121" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Despite the amendment made by item 28 of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act, section 121, as in force immediately before the commencement of that item, continues to apply in relation to the termination of an employee’s employment if any of the following occurred before that commencement: (a) the termination of the employee; (b) any other termination covered by that section as amended that caused the employer to become a small business employer.  Schedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act" ;
    cof:pageNumber "83"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-93 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "93 Application of amendments—regulated labour hire arrangement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-93 ;
    values:originalText "orders Application of requirement to pay protected rate of pay (1) Section 306F of the amended Act (protected rate of pay payable to employees if a regulated labour hire arrangement order is in force) applies on and after 1 November 2024 regardless of whether any agreement resulting in the performance of work by a regulated employee is entered into before, on or after that day. Anti-avoidance provisions apply retrospectively in relation to certain conduct and schemes (2) Division 4 of Part 2-7A of the amended Act (anti-avoidance) applies, on and after the introduction day, in relation to: (a) conduct engaged in; or (b) a scheme that is entered into, begun to be carried out or carried out; on or after the introduction day. (3) In this section: introduction day means the day on which the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes) Bill 2023 was introduced into the Parliament.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes) Act" ;
    skos:definition "orders Application of requirement to pay protected rate of pay (1) Section 306F of the amended Act (protected rate of pay payable to employees if a regulated labour hire arrangement order is in force) applies on and after 1 November 2024 regardless of whether any agreement resulting in the performance of work by a regulated employee is entered into before, on or after that day. Anti-avoidance provisions apply retrospectively in relation to certain conduct and schemes (2) Division 4 of Part 2-7A of the amended Act (anti-avoidance) applies, on and after the introduction day, in relation to: (a) conduct engaged in; or (b) a scheme that is entered into, begun to be carried out or carried out; on or after the introduction day. (3) In this section: introduction day means the day on which the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes) Bill 2023 was introduced into the Parliament.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes) Act"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "55e45f34fcb1e6b8c30d5bdc9ea413354e9fb08182ea2da2885b85f8872e675d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-93-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-93-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-93-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.84" .
doc:sch-1-sec-93 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "93 Application of amendments—regulated labour hire arrangement" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "orders Application of requirement to pay protected rate of pay (1) Section 306F of the amended Act (protected rate of pay payable to employees if a regulated labour hire arrangement order is in force) applies on and after 1 November 2024 regardless of whether any agreement resulting in the performance of work by a regulated employee is entered into before, on or after that day. Anti-avoidance provisions apply retrospectively in relation to certain conduct and schemes (2) Division 4 of Part 2-7A of the amended Act (anti-avoidance) applies, on and after the introduction day, in relation to: (a) conduct engaged in; or (b) a scheme that is entered into, begun to be carried out or carried out; on or after the introduction day. (3) In this section: introduction day means the day on which the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes) Bill 2023 was introduced into the Parliament.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes) Act" ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer .

