concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-103 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "103 Transitional provision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-103 ;
    values:originalText "For the purposes of applying section 66L of this Act during the period beginning when this clause commences and ending when Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act commences, the reference to “this Division” in that provision is taken to include a reference to that Division as amended by that Part.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Main amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 16 Amendments made by Part 4 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 3 Clause 104 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "For the purposes of applying section 66L of this Act during the period beginning when this clause commences and ending when Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act commences, the reference to “this Division” in that provision is taken to include a reference to that Division as amended by that Part.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Main amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 16 Amendments made by Part 4 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 3 Clause 104 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "355475bd02d2c4639388655c4fefd1950384ed7961232e1abb5265558a7ccb1b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Transitional provision for applying section 66L of the Act during a specific period." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.94" ;
    cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-103-norm .
concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-103-norm a values:Undertaking ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-103 ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-1-sec-103 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "103 Transitional provision" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "For the purposes of applying section 66L of this Act during the period beginning when this clause commences and ending when Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act commences, the reference to “this Division” in that provision is taken to include a reference to that Division as amended by that Part.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Main amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 16 Amendments made by Part 4 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 3 Clause 104 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-104 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "104 Replacement agreements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-104 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subsections 58(4) and (5), as inserted by the amending Act, apply in relation to single-enterprise agreements made after the commencement of Part 4 of Schedule 1 to that Act, whether the single interest employer agreement or supported bargaining agreement was made before or after that commencement. (2) Section 180B and subsection 240A(4), as inserted by the amending Act, apply in relation to single interest employer agreements and supported bargaining agreements whether made before or after the commencement of Part 4 of Schedule 1 to that Act. (3) Subsections 236(1B) and 238(2), as inserted by the amending Act, apply in relation to applications made after the commencement of Part 4 of Schedule 1 to that Act, whether the single interest employer agreement or supported bargaining agreement was made before or after that commencement." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subsections 58(4) and (5), as inserted by the amending Act, apply in relation to single-enterprise agreements made after the commencement of Part 4 of Schedule 1 to that Act, whether the single interest employer agreement or supported bargaining agreement was made before or after that commencement. (2) Section 180B and subsection 240A(4), as inserted by the amending Act, apply in relation to single interest employer agreements and supported bargaining agreements whether made before or after the commencement of Part 4 of Schedule 1 to that Act. (3) Subsections 236(1B) and 238(2), as inserted by the amending Act, apply in relation to applications made after the commencement of Part 4 of Schedule 1 to that Act, whether the single interest employer agreement or supported bargaining agreement was made before or after that commencement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "16f1f71969b0ca6562f203e0827b9a6e06812a039f134c588977b4ffc399a4b1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "95"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-104-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-104-ss-2 ;
