concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-111 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "111 Application of amendments to intractable bargaining workplace"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-111 ;
    values:originalText "determinations made before commencement (1) This clause applies in relation to an intractable bargaining workplace determination made before the commencement of Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act (the original determination). (2) On application by an employer, employee or employee organisation covered by the original determination, the FWC must make a determination (a variation) varying the original determination where required so as to give effect to the provisions to which clause 110 applies.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Main amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 16 Amendments made by Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 5 Clause 111 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (3) An application under subclause (2) must be made before the end of the period of 12 months commencing on the day Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act commences. (4) The FWC may make a variation despite paragraph 603(3)(c). (5) Any variation must be made by a Full Bench. (6) A variation operates from the day specified by the FWC in the variation, which must not be a day before the variation is made.  Schedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act" ;
    skos:definition "determinations made before commencement (1) This clause applies in relation to an intractable bargaining workplace determination made before the commencement of Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act (the original determination). (2) On application by an employer, employee or employee organisation covered by the original determination, the FWC must make a determination (a variation) varying the original determination where required so as to give effect to the provisions to which clause 110 applies.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Main amendments made by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 16 Amendments made by Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act  Division 5 Clause 111 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (3) An application under subclause (2) must be made before the end of the period of 12 months commencing on the day Part 5A of Schedule 1 to the amending Act commences. (4) The FWC may make a variation despite paragraph 603(3)(c). (5) Any variation must be made by a Full Bench. (6) A variation operates from the day specified by the FWC in the variation, which must not be a day before the variation is made.  Schedule 1  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7c39c69636d3942369d5195567e22b4d07d54ac0af073602f315deea8a7a8137" ;
    cof:pageNumber "98"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-111-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-111-ss-2 ;
