concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-123 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "123 Definitions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-123 ;
    values:originalText "In this Part: amended Act means this Act as amended by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024. amending Act means the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024. commencement means the commencement of item 238 of Part 16 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act. old Act means this Act as in force immediately before commencement.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Amendments made by Part 16 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 18 Transitional provisions  Division 2 Clause 124 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "In this Part: amended Act means this Act as amended by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024. amending Act means the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024. commencement means the commencement of item 238 of Part 16 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act. old Act means this Act as in force immediately before commencement.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Amendments made by Part 16 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 18 Transitional provisions  Division 2 Clause 124 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fbc6b787af1d800d3b4daaadfa05af0ff99d2039bd24ef983a71fe027ca3e3a2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "112"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definitions for amended Act and commencement" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.112" ;
    cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-123-norm .
concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-123-norm a values:Undertaking ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-123 ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-1-sec-123 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "123 Definitions" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "In this Part: amended Act means this Act as amended by the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024. amending Act means the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024. commencement means the commencement of item 238 of Part 16 of Schedule 1 to the amending Act. old Act means this Act as in force immediately before commencement.  Application, saving and transitional provisions relating to amendments of this Act Schedule 1 Amendments made by Part 16 of Schedule 1 to the Fair Work Legislation Amendment (Closing Loopholes No. 2) Act 2024  Part 18 Transitional provisions  Division 2 Clause 124 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "112"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-124 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "124 Unfair deactivation and unfair termination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-124 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Part 3A-3 (unfair deactivation or unfair termination of regulated workers) applies to a deactivation or termination that occurs after commencement. (2) For the purposes of determining under paragraph 536LD(c) whether an employee-like worker has been performing work for a period of at least 6 months, a period or periods before commencement are not to be counted. (3) For the purposes of determining under paragraph 536LE(c) whether a regulated road transport contractor has been performing work for a period of at least 6 months, a period or periods before commencement are not to be counted." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Part 3A-3 (unfair deactivation or unfair termination of regulated workers) applies to a deactivation or termination that occurs after commencement. (2) For the purposes of determining under paragraph 536LD(c) whether an employee-like worker has been performing work for a period of at least 6 months, a period or periods before commencement are not to be counted. (3) For the purposes of determining under paragraph 536LE(c) whether a regulated road transport contractor has been performing work for a period of at least 6 months, a period or periods before commencement are not to be counted."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1af5f439ae198895b971d0869eddddac728e19d20e75b79fb3a104ca47bcb9aa" ;
    cof:pageNumber "113"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-124-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-124-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sch-1-sec-124-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.113" .
